1
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:38,360
But otherwise the Finnish economy has been bleak.
A bit like elsewhere too.

2
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:44,720
Everything that happens with industrial production, growth, the prospects has been quite weak.

3
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:50,920
But you still see resilience during the latter part of the year.
What are you saying?

4
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:59,440
If we look at individual companies, they are starting to be very cheaply priced.

5
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:04,800
Finland has had two years of downward stock prices.

6
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:11,680
At the same time, the companies' situation is not completely hopeless.

7
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:19,400
Next year, we expect a profit growth of 5-7 % if we look at index level.

8
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,920
And at the same time, these companies are very cheap.

9
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:30,120
So if you look a little longer you should own the Finnish stock exchange as well.

10
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,880
Could it be a good position to come in if you don't have ...?

11
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:37,880
Not getting in at the top is always nice.

12
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:55,320
Fed has done its thing, the ECB has probably done its thing.

13
00:04:55,400 --> 00:05:01,440
At the same time we see that the growth figures are getting a little lower-

14
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:06,240
-in the start of next year.
If it becomes a "soft landing" in the US, we will see ...

15
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:10,160
But clearly lower growth.

16
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:15,280
And it is already priced that the policy rates will be lower in 2024.

17
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:19,160
It should stimulate the economy to some extent.

18
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:26,920
You started working in the financial market before 1992.

19
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:33,160
You are a bit back in a world with a lot of uncertainty-

20
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:36,560
-But where interest rates are also interesting again.

21
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,800
-Just.
-Do you other synergies?

22
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:44,360
That's right.
In 1992 I started as an interest portfolio manager in a Finnish company-

23
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:30,440
And though the policy rate drops so ...

24
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:34,480
There are so much loans that need to be financed again-

25
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:42,280
-So it may be that the risk premium, the price they have to pay for new loan-

26
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,560
-will rise.

27
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:48,280
But can't it be that you now get in at the top?

28
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:54,400
That those who allocate about their portfolios, that they invest errors at the top in the interest rate market-

29
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:58,240
-and that they get a lower return.
Isn't that risk?

30
00:15:58,320 --> 00:16:02,560
As an investor, if you have a little longer horizon and place in corporate loans ...

31
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:05,760
Then this is a great buying position.

32
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:09,520
But for companies ... we had an example here in Finland.

33
